## Why This Is Asked
This assesses practical, beginner-friendly end-to-end testing skills focusing on input validation, idempotency, queueing, rate limiting, and privacy in logs; uses realistic dataflow rather than theory.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing with real components vs mocks
- Idempotency keys for duplicate requests
- Rate-limiting and concurrency testing
- Log scrubbing and PII protection
- CI reproducibility with fixtures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Jest + supertest skeleton for /feedback endpoint
const request = require('supertest');
const app = require('../src/app');

test('idempotent submission', async () => {
  const payload = { user: 'alice', feedback: 'great', idempotencyKey: 'abc-123' };
  await request(app).post('/feedback').send(payload).expect(201);
  // second attempt with same key should be treated as duplicate
  await request(app).post('/feedback').send(payload).expect(409);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you adapt tests for non-deterministic services (e.g., occasional DB hiccups)?
- What strategies would you use to measure and reduce test flakiness in CI?
